<title>USA: Scherer customer gets FDA approval.</title>
<headline>Scherer customer gets FDA approval.</headline>
<dateline>TROY, Mich. 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>R.P. Scherer said its Monday its customer, Schering-Plough Corp, received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to sell Clariten RediTabs.</p>
<p>Clariten RediTabs use Scherer's Zydis instantly dissolving technology, the company said. Clariten is the most prescribed antihistamine in the world, according to Scherer.</p>
<p>Including the Clariten tabs, there are now six prescription products being marketed around the world that use the Zydis technology, Scherer said.</p>
<p>Scherer is a major producer of soft gelatin capsules.</p>
</text>
